        { type: "multipleChoice", question: "Which EMDR bilateral stimulation adaptation involves clients tapping alternating knees or shoulders?", options: ["Therapist-guided screen tracking", "Butterfly hug", "Audio-based bilateral tones", "Virtual light bar application"], correctAnswer: 1, explanation: "The butterfly hug involves crossing arms and alternately tapping shoulders or knees. It is the most commonly used telehealth EMDR adaptation because it is client-controlled and not dependent on video quality." }
